Auto Ticket Classification Using Flow Designer
8.Demonstration Objective
The demonstration shows how a newly created ticket is automatically processed by the Flow Designer workflow.

8.2 Demonstration Steps
Demo video link:https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DtOf1HlBEul17asW-K3ScR6ZJCY14Z4m/view?usp=sharing
Step 1
Create a new ticket.

Example:

Short Description:
"Unable to connect to Wi-Fi"

Step 2
Submit the ticket.

Step 3
The Flow Designer trigger detects the newly created ticket.

Step 4
The flow evaluates the ticket information.

Step 5
The classification condition identifies the ticket as a network-related issue.

Step 6
The flow automatically updates:

Category: Network Issue

Assignment Group: Network Support

Step 7
A work note can be added:

"Ticket automatically classified and routed using Flow Designer."

Step 8
The final ticket is displayed to demonstrate that classification and assignment occurred automatically.
